    "title": "If you hear a bunch of screaming by the Trinity River this Sunday, this is why. - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Caitlin Clark ,\n1 days ago Right now on Instagram, there’s a bit of food-related drama brewing between Roni Proctor (@dinnerreinvented), Oloyo, and probably the local chef community at large. I’m not equipped to comment on that. But in a less viral corner of the internet, one Dallas man is hoping to unite rather than divide. His mission: to gather a group at Trammell Crow Park for the inaugural Dallas Yell Club and scream into the void this Sunday at 6 pm. It’s kind of like that Chicago Scream Club, but instead of letting out a primal yell over Lake Michigan, you’ll be hollering over the Trinity River. The therapeutic benefits of screaming aren’t discerning about bodies of water. Read full article",
